Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @PACKAGE_VERSION@-1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Robert Paleka <paleka@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: zlib1g, libzstd1, snapraid (>= 15.0), systemd
Recommends: mergerfs, parted, fdisk, util-linux, e2fsprogs, xfsprogs, btrfs-progs, rsync, smartmontools, curl
Conflicts: snapraid-daemon
Replaces: snapraid-daemon
Provides: snapraid-daemon
Description: SnapRAID Daemon with the Storage page (unofficial fork)
 This is an unofficial fork of SnapRAID Daemon by Andrea Mazzoleni. It adds a
 Storage page to the web UI, to set up and maintain a SnapRAID array, with or
 without a mergerfs pool. It replaces the snapraid-daemon package and uses the
 same program, service and configuration file.
 .
 SnapRAID Daemon is a lightweight background service that transforms manual parity
 tasks into an automated workflow. It integrates directly with SnapRAID to
 coordinate sync and scrub operations via intelligent scheduling, ensuring your
 protection stays current without manual command-line intervention.
 The service features a built-in Web UI and a comprehensive REST API, providing
 both visual oversight and programmatic control. While the dashboard offers
 real-time status and health alerts, the API enables seamless integration into
 external monitoring stacks for persistent and reliable data protection.
Homepage: https://github.com/paleka/snapraid-daemon
